  "Question": "A tank initially contains 100 L of water. Water flows out at 5 L per minute, and after \\(t\\) minutes, the amount remaining is \\((100-5t)\\) L. At which minute is the tank completely emptied?",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "20",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "When the amount remaining is 0, \\(100-5t=0\\). Solving gives \\(t=20\\), so the tank is completely emptied at the 20th minute.\n\nAlternative method 1: Count one-minute amounts\n\nThe tank empties once all \\(100\\) L have flowed out. Each minute removes \\(5\\) L, so the number of one-minute amounts in \\(100\\) L is\n\\[\n100\\div5=20.\n\\]\nTherefore, the tank is completely empty after \\(20\\) minutes.",
